WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.197
Advanced S Q L is mostly about controlling two things: intermediate results and row context.

00:00:06.197 --> 00:00:14.332
A common table expression gives a useful name to one stage of a larger query.

00:00:14.332 --> 00:00:18.322
That makes a complicated query easier to read one step at a time.

00:00:18.322 --> 00:00:21.112
A window function does something different.

00:00:21.112 --> 00:00:31.142
It lets the current row use information from related rows while still keeping the current row in the result.

00:00:31.142 --> 00:00:39.347
For example, we can keep every employee row and place the department average salary beside each employee.

00:00:39.347 --> 00:00:45.617
Or we can keep every admission and place the previous admission date beside the current one.

00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:53.457
That is the main idea of this module: add analytical context without losing track of the row grain.
